!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = D425
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: D425 sensitive
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: DMSO
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = ip antibody: H3
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Sensitive and drug-tolerant D425 and D458 were passaged in DMSO or JQ1 (1 µM) for 24 hours. Sheared chromatin from each cell line was subjected to ChIP-sequencing as previously described62 , enriching for H3K27ac (Cell Signaling Technologies, 8173S)), H3K4me3 (Cell Signaling Technologies, 9751S), Histone H3 (Cell Signaling 4499S) and BRD4 (Bethyl, A301-985A100). ChIP libraries were indexed, pooled and sequenced on Illumina Hi-seq-2000 sequencers.
!Sample_data_processing = Raw data was aligned to the human reference genome Hg19 using Picard tools (http://broadinstitute.github.io/picard/). Raw sequencing data was mapped to the reference genome using bowtie2 version 2.2.1 with parameters -p 4 -k 1.
!Sample_data_processing = Peaks were called using MACS version 1.4.2 over an input control. Reads were extended 200-bp and normalized to read-density in units of reads per million mapped reads per bp (rpm/bp).
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: Hg19
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: BED peak files
